    {
      "question": "e-11026",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "dc2f3a451dc1eef6a912d0def44dd1e7294ad56747bfe9290f4dab2a7f141149",
      "new_sha256": "469022e6b31a2e5509b4df2a57808345ed4c1ee5173a17417693e08901273b94",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-11026",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202y} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(3x\\operatorname{ln}\u2061y+2y{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(3x\\operatorname{ln}\u2061y)+\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(2y{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =3x\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061y)+2{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(y) \\\\  & =3x\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}+2{e}^{x}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{3x}{y}+2{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/example-11026.json",
          "file_sha256": "4f5c8ce0cadc22a413b0458a351aca559b1f72869925f987ce1f8c0c3dc6fd57"
        }
